WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.509 --> 00:00:05.590
For Groomer Books, one twenty-dollar plan covers all three top jobs.

2
00:00:05.626 --> 00:00:07.254
Here's the example.

3
00:00:07.274 --> 00:00:09.654
The tier is twenty dollars a month.

4
00:00:09.674 --> 00:00:21.507
The top jobs from the delegation map are overdue-invoice reminders at seventy-five minutes a week, Instagram posts at forty-five, and sorting receipts at forty.

5
00:00:21.527 --> 00:00:27.907
All three are writing and sorting jobs, so one main office handles them: Claude Pro.

6
00:00:27.927 --> 00:00:32.515
It drafts the reminders and the posts, and sorts receipts in a project.

7
00:00:32.535 --> 00:00:38.881
The gap is posting itself, which stays manual, because nothing publishes without the founder.

8
00:00:38.926 --> 00:00:42.356
No two plans overlap, because there's only one.

9
00:00:42.376 --> 00:00:48.778
The always-on agent is the Claude Duet waitlist, after checking the account is in the US.

10
00:00:48.827 --> 00:00:53.282
Specialists wait until the main office has had a week of real use.

11
00:00:53.302 --> 00:00:57.068
And the decision has a review date, ninety days out.

12
00:00:57.094 --> 00:01:00.197
That's a stack decision you can act on today.

